# Probate and Administration Act 1934 — the grant machinery

## Section 2 — Interpretation

<!-- l4: decide:s 2 — the definitions the grant machinery reads -->

**1.** S 2 — the definitions the grant machinery reads if—

    (a) “prescribed form” means the form prescribed by rules made under any law for the time being in force relating to the courts;;

    (b) “probate action” means a cause or matter in which a probate application is contested by any person, and includes any application to alter or revoke the grant of any probate or letters of administration;;

    (c) “probate application” means an application for a grant of probate or letters of administration, and “probate applicant” shall be construed accordingly;;

    (d) “Public Trustee” means the Public Trustee appointed under the Public Trustee Act 1915 and includes a Deputy Public Trustee and an Assistant Public Trustee appointed under that Act;;

    (e) “registrar” means the registrar of the Family Justice Courts;; and

    (f) “will” includes any codicil or other testamentary document..

## The further facts on which the grant machinery turns

<!-- l4: declare:The further facts on which the grant machinery turns -->

**2.** In this Act, “The further facts on which the grant machinery turns” means a record consisting of—

    (a) “the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (b) “the Family Court thinks fit to require such security”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (c) “there is danger that the property may be wasted”, being a BOOLEAN;

    (d) “it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate”, being a BOOLEAN; and

    (e) “the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property”, being a BOOLEAN.

## Reading the shared ontology — the helpers the sections below share

<!-- l4: decide:the individual in -->

**3.** In relation to a Person or corporation “pc”, the individual in means consider the case distinctions of pc :  when an individual has p then JUST with p. in any other case NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:an individual, within the meaning of section 6(2) -->

**4.** In relation to a Person or corporation “pc”, an individual, within the meaning of section 6(2) means isJust with the individual in with pc.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(6) — a trust corporation -->

**5.** In relation to a Person or corporation “pc”, s 6(6) — a trust corporation means consider the case distinctions of pc :  when the Public Trustee has  then TRUE. when a corporation licensed as a trust company under the Trust Companies Act 2005 has n then TRUE. in any other case FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:is the individual whose reference is -->

**6.** In relation to a Person or corporation “pc” and a STRING “the reference”, is the individual whose reference is means consider the case distinctions of pc :  when an individual has p then p's the reference for this person is equal to the reference. in any other case FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:has died -->

**7.** In relation to a Person “p”, has died means consider the case distinctions of p's vital status :  when living has  then FALSE. in any other case TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the date of death of -->

**8.** In relation to a Person “p”, the date of death of means consider the case distinctions of p's vital status :  when died on has d then JUST with d. in any other case NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:survives -->

**9.** In relation to a Person “a” and a Person “b”, survives means consider the case distinctions of a's vital status :  when living has  then TRUE. when dead, the date of death not known has  then FALSE. when died on has da then consider the case distinctions of b's vital status :  when died on has db then _ is after _ with da and db. in any other case FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:is an infant on -->

**10.** In relation to a Person “p” and a DATE “the date”, is an infant on means consider the case distinctions of p's the date on which the person attains the age of majority :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has m then _ is before _ with the date and m.

<!-- l4: decide:a “child” within the meaning of section 3 of the Intestate Succession Act 1967 -->

**11.** In relation to a Child “c”, a “child” within the meaning of section 3 of the Intestate Succession Act 1967 if—

    (a) c's a legitimate child of the person whose child he is; or

    (b) c's adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam.

<!-- l4: decide:the descendants of -->

**12.** In relation to a Person “p”, the descendants of means concat with map with the child and his descendants and p's children.

<!-- l4: decide:the child and his descendants -->

**13.** In relation to a Child “c”, the child and his descendants means if a “child” within the meaning of section 3 of the Intestate Succession Act 1967 with c, then c's the child followed by the descendants of with c's the child; otherwise, EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the next of kin of the deceased -->

**14.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, the next of kin of the deceased means filter with given p then _ survives _ with p and d's the deceased and the classes from which the next of kin are drawn with d.

<!-- l4: decide:the classes from which the next of kin are drawn -->

**15.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, the classes from which the next of kin are drawn means concat with list of the descendants of with d's the deceased, maybeToList with d's the family's the father of the deceased, maybeToList with d's the family's the mother of the deceased, map with given r then r's the relative and d's the family's the brothers and sisters of the deceased, concat with map with given r then the descendants of with r's the relative and d's the family's the brothers and sisters of the deceased, d's the family's the grandparents of the deceased and map with given r then r's the relative and d's the family's the uncles and aunts of the deceased.

<!-- l4: decide:a marriage leaving a husband or widow -->

**16.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Marriage “m”, a marriage leaving a husband or widow if—

    (a) m's subsisting at the death of the deceased, in the sense of not dissolved or annulled before the death; and

    (b) _ survives _ with m's the spouse and d's the deceased.

<!-- l4: decide:the husband or widow of the deceased -->

**17.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, the husband or widow of the deceased means map with given m then m's the spouse and filter with given m then a marriage leaving a husband or widow with d and m and d's the family's the marriages of the deceased.

<!-- l4: decide:the value of the property in Singapore -->

**18.** In relation to an Estate “e”, the value of the property in Singapore means the sum of e's the value of the movable property situated in Singapore and e's the value of the immovable property situated in Singapore.

<!-- l4: decide:a personal representative -->

**19.** In relation to a Grantee “gr”, a personal representative if—

    (a) gr's the capacity in which the grant is made is equal to as executor; or

    (b) gr's the capacity in which the grant is made is equal to as administrator.

<!-- l4: decide:the personal representatives of the estate -->

**20.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, the personal representatives of the estate means filter with given gr then a personal representative with gr and concat with map with given g then g's the grantees and filter with given g then not g's revoked and d's the grants made in respect of the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:the personal representatives of the estate still living -->

**21.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, the personal representatives of the estate still living means filter with given gr then not this grantee has died with gr and the personal representatives of the estate with d.

## Part 2 — Renunciation

<!-- l4: decide:s 5(1) — the person so renouncing is precluded from applying thereafter for probate or letters of administration -->

**22.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “the person has renounced, whether expressly under section 3 or constructively under section 4”, s 5(1) — the person so renouncing is precluded from applying thereafter for probate or letters of administration means the person has renounced, whether expressly under section 3 or constructively under section 4.

<!-- l4: decide:s 5(1) — precluded from applying thereafter for probate or letters of administration -->

**23.** In relation to an Executor appointed by a will “x”, s 5(1) — precluded from applying thereafter for probate or letters of administration means s 5(1) — the person so renouncing is precluded from applying thereafter for probate or letters of administration with x's has renounced the right to act as such.

# Part 3 — Grant of probate or letters of administration

## Section 6 — Provisions as to number of personal representatives

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(1) — granted to more than 4 persons in respect of the same property -->

**24.** In relation to a Grant “g”, s 6(1) — granted to more than 4 persons in respect of the same property means count with g's the grantees is greater than 4.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(2) — there is a minority -->

**25.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 6(2) — there is a minority means any with given i then _ is an infant on _ with i's the infant and the date and d's the infants concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(2) — a life interest arises under the will -->

**26.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 6(2) — a life interest arises under the will means consider the case distinctions of d's the will :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has w then not null with w's the life interests arising under the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(2) — the requirement as to the grantees is engaged -->

**27.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 6(2) — the requirement as to the grantees is engaged if—

    (a) if there is a minority or if a life interest arises under the will,;

    (b) s 6(2) — there is a minority with d and the date; or

    (c) s 6(2) — a life interest arises under the will with d.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(2) — granted either to a trust corporation, with or without an individual, or to not less than 2 individuals -->

**28.** In relation to a Grant “g”, s 6(2) — granted either to a trust corporation, with or without an individual, or to not less than 2 individuals if—

    (a) either to a trust corporation, with or without an individual,;

    (b) any with given gr then s 6(6) — a trust corporation with gr's the grantee and g's the grantees; or

    (c) count with filter with given gr then an individual, within the meaning of section 6(2) with gr's the grantee and g's the grantees is at least 2.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(2) — the grant is one of the grants section 6(2) governs -->

**29.** In relation to a Grant “g”, s 6(2) — the grant is one of the grants section 6(2) governs if—

    (a) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration; or

    (b) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration with the will annexed.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(2) — the grant complies with section 6(2) -->

**30.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grant “g” and a DATE “the date”, s 6(2) — the grant complies with section 6(2) if—

    (a) it is not the case that—

        (i) s 6(2) — the grant is one of the grants section 6(2) governs with g; and

        (ii) s 6(2) — the requirement as to the grantees is engaged with d and the date; or

    (b) s 6(2) — granted either to a trust corporation, with or without an individual, or to not less than 2 individuals with g.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(3) — prima facie evidence of a minority or life interest (not encoded) -->

**31.** S 6(3) — prima facie evidence of a minority or life interest (not encoded) means The court in granting letters of administration may act on such prima facie evidence, furnished by the applicant or any other person, as to whether or not there is a minority or life interest, as may be prescribed by rules made under any written law for the time being in force relating to the courts..

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(4) — a life interest subsists -->

**32.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 6(4) — a life interest subsists means consider the case distinctions of d's the will :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has w then any with given li then not has died with li's the life tenant and w's the life interests arising under the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary -->

**33.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Person “p”, s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary means consider the case distinctions of d's the will :  when JUST has w then not null with filter with given dp then dp's beneficial and the dispositions to this person with d and p's the reference for this person or any with given li then li's the life tenant's the reference for this person is equal to p's the reference for this person and w's the life interests arising under the will. when NOTHING has  then s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin with d and p's the reference for this person.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(4) — there is a minority of a beneficiary -->

**34.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 6(4) — there is a minority of a beneficiary means any with given i then _ is an infant on _ with i's the infant and the date and s 6(4) — this person is a beneficiary with d and i's the infant and d's the infants concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative -->

**35.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 6(4) — the window in which the court may appoint an additional personal representative if—

    (a) If there is only one personal representative (not being a trust corporation);

    (b) count with the personal representatives of the estate still living with d is equal to 1;

    (c) all with given gr then not s 6(6) — a trust corporation with gr's the grantee and the personal representatives of the estate still living with d;

    (d) then, during the minority of a beneficiary or the subsistence of a life interest;

    (e) any of the following applies—

        (i) s 6(4) — there is a minority of a beneficiary with d and the date; or

        (ii) s 6(4) — a life interest subsists with d;

    (f) and until the estate is fully administered,; and

    (g) it is not the case that d's the estate's fully administered.

<!-- l4: decide:s 6(5) — this section applies to the grant -->

**36.** In relation to a Grant “g”, s 6(5) — this section applies to the grant means consider the case distinctions of g's the date of the grant :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has dg then _ is after _ with dg and YMD with 1935, 1 and 1.

## Section 8 — Grant of probate

<!-- l4: decide:s 8(1) — probate may be granted to this person as an executor appointed by a will -->

**37.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a STRING “the reference”, s 8(1) — probate may be granted to this person as an executor appointed by a will means consider the case distinctions of d's the will :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has w then any with given x then x's the executor's the reference for this person is equal to the reference and w's the executors appointed by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 8(3) — probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed, subject to section 6 -->

**38.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Grant “g”, s 8(3) — probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed, subject to section 6 if—

    (a) Subject to section 6,;

    (b) it is not the case that s 6(1) — granted to more than 4 persons in respect of the same property with g;

    (c) where more than one person is appointed an executor by a will,;

    (d) count with the executors appointed by the will of the deceased with d is greater than 1;

    (e) probate may be granted to one or more of the persons so appointed,;

    (f) all with given gr then s 8(1) — probate may be granted to this person as an executor appointed by a will with d and the reference of the grantee with gr and g's the grantees; and

    (g) without prejudice to a subsequent application by another or others of them for further grant or grants..

<!-- l4: decide:the reference of the grantee -->

**39.** In relation to a Grantee “gr”, the reference of the grantee means consider the case distinctions of the individual in with gr's the grantee :  when JUST has p then p's the reference for this person. when NOTHING has  then.

## Sections 9 to 11 — where the will is lost, destroyed, or proved abroad

<!-- l4: declare:The probate that may be granted where the will cannot be produced -->

**40.** In this Act, “The probate that may be granted where the will cannot be produced” means one of the following—

    (a) “no probate may be granted under section 9”;

    (b) “probate of that copy or draft, limited until the original is admitted to probate”; or

    (c) “probate of the contents of the will, limited until the original is admitted to probate”.

<!-- l4: decide:s 9 — probate of copy or draft, or of contents -->

**41.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “a will has been lost or mislaid after the death of the testator”, a BOOLEAN “a will cannot for any sufficient reason be produced”, a BOOLEAN “a copy or draft thereof is produced”, a BOOLEAN “it appears that the copy or draft is identical in terms with the original” and a BOOLEAN “the contents of the will can be sufficiently established”, s 9 — probate of copy or draft, or of contents means if not a will has been lost or mislaid after the death of the testator or a will cannot for any sufficient reason be produced then no probate may be granted under section 9 if a copy or draft thereof is produced and it appears that the copy or draft is identical in terms with the original then probate of that copy or draft, limited until the original is admitted to probate if not a copy or draft thereof is produced and the contents of the will can be sufficiently established then probate of the contents of the will, limited until the original is admitted to probate otherwise no probate may be granted under section 9.

<!-- l4: decide:s 10 — probate may be granted of a copy or draft thereof, or of the contents thereof -->

**42.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “a will has been destroyed”, a BOOLEAN “the will was destroyed by the act or with the consent of the testator” and a BOOLEAN “the copy, draft or contents can be sufficiently established”, s 10 — probate may be granted of a copy or draft thereof, or of the contents thereof if—

    (a) Where a will has been destroyed,;

    (b) a will has been destroyed;

    (c) otherwise than by the act or with the consent of the testator,;

    (d) it is not the case that the will was destroyed by the act or with the consent of the testator;

    (e) if they can be sufficiently established.; and

    (f) the copy, draft or contents can be sufficiently established.

<!-- l4: decide:s 11 — administration with copy annexed of authenticated copy of will proved abroad -->

**43.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “a will has been proved and deposited in a court of competent jurisdiction situated beyond the limits of Singapore” and a BOOLEAN “a properly authenticated copy of the will is produced”, s 11 — administration with copy annexed of authenticated copy of will proved abroad means if a will has been proved and deposited in a court of competent jurisdiction situated beyond the limits of Singapore and a properly authenticated copy of the will is produced, then list of probate and letters of administration with the will annexed; otherwise, EMPTY.

## Sections 12 and 16 — a codicil propounded after a grant

<!-- l4: declare:The consequence of a codicil propounded after a grant -->

**44.** In this Act, “The consequence of a codicil propounded after a grant” means one of the following—

    (a) “nothing follows under section 12”;

    (b) “separate probate may be granted of the codicil”; or

    (c) “the probate shall be revoked, and a new probate shall be granted of the will and codicil together”.

<!-- l4: decide:s 12 — codicil propounded after probate -->

**45.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “a codicil of the will is propounded after probate has been granted” and a BOOLEAN “the codicil expressly or impliedly revokes the appointment of any executor to whom probate has been granted”, s 12 — codicil propounded after probate means if not a codicil of the will is propounded after probate has been granted then nothing follows under section 12 if the codicil expressly or impliedly revokes the appointment of any executor to whom probate has been granted then the probate shall be revoked, and a new probate shall be granted of the will and codicil together otherwise separate probate may be granted of the codicil.

<!-- l4: decide:s 16 — codicil propounded after grant of letters of administration -->

**46.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “a codicil of the will is propounded after letters of administration with the will annexed have been granted” and a BOOLEAN “the codicil expressly or impliedly revokes the appointment of any executor to whom the grant has been made”, s 16 — codicil propounded after grant of letters of administration means s 12 — codicil propounded after probate with a codicil of the will is propounded after letters of administration with the will annexed have been granted and the codicil expressly or impliedly revokes the appointment of any executor to whom the grant has been made.

## Section 13 — Letters of administration with the will annexed, on failure of executors

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1)(a) — no executor is appointed by a will -->

**47.** In relation to a Will “w”, s 13(1)(a) — no executor is appointed by a will means null with w's the executors appointed by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1)(b) — this executor is legally incapable of acting as such -->

**48.** In relation to an Executor appointed by a will “x” and a DATE “the date”, s 13(1)(b) — this executor is legally incapable of acting as such if—

    (a) x's legally incapable of acting as such, otherwise than under section 21(1) or section 22(1);

    (b) _ is an infant on _ with x's the executor and the date; or

    (c) x's the executor's lacks mental capacity (within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act 2008) to make decisions with respect to the management and administration of the person's property and affairs.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1)(b) — this executor is disqualified -->

**49.** In relation to an Executor appointed by a will “x” and a DATE “the date”, s 13(1)(b) — this executor is disqualified if—

    (a) s 13(1)(b) — this executor is legally incapable of acting as such with x and the date; or

    (b) x's has renounced the right to act as such.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such -->

**50.** In relation to a Will “w” and a DATE “the date”, s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such means all with given x then s 13(1)(b) — this executor is disqualified with x and the date and w's the executors appointed by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1)(c) — no executor survives the testator -->

**51.** In relation to a Will “w”, s 13(1)(c) — no executor survives the testator if it is not the case that any with given x then _ survives _ with x's the executor and w's the testator and w's the executors appointed by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:this grantee is this executor, taking as executor -->

**52.** In relation to a Grantee “gr” and an Executor appointed by a will “x”, this grantee is this executor, taking as executor if—

    (a) _ is the individual whose reference is _ with gr's the grantee and x's the executor's the reference for this person; and

    (b) gr's the capacity in which the grant is made is equal to as executor.

<!-- l4: decide:the grant was made in this executor's lifetime -->

**53.** In relation to a Grant “g” and an Executor appointed by a will “x”, the grant was made in this executor's lifetime means consider the case distinctions of the date of death of with x's the executor :  when NOTHING has  then not has died with x's the executor. when JUST has dx then consider the case distinctions of g's the date of the grant :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has dg then not _ is after _ with dg and dx.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1)(d) — this executor obtained probate -->

**54.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and an Executor appointed by a will “x”, s 13(1)(d) — this executor obtained probate means any with given g then a grant of probate obtained by this executor in his lifetime with g and x and d's the grants made in respect of the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:a grant of probate obtained by this executor in his lifetime -->

**55.** In relation to a Grant “g” and an Executor appointed by a will “x”, a grant of probate obtained by this executor in his lifetime if—

    (a) g's the kind of grant is equal to probate;

    (b) it is not the case that g's revoked;

    (c) any with given gr then this grantee is this executor, taking as executor with gr and x and g's the grantees; and

    (d) the grant was made in this executor's lifetime with g and x.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1)(d) — this executor died before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased -->

**56.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and an Executor appointed by a will “x”, s 13(1)(d) — this executor died before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased if—

    (a) has died with x's the executor; and

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) it is not the case that s 13(1)(d) — this executor obtained probate with d and x; or

        (ii) x's does not have administered all the estate of the deceased.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased -->

**57.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Will “w”, s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased means all with given x then s 13(1)(d) — this executor died before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased with d and x and w's the executors appointed by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1)(e) — the executors appointed by any will do not appear and extract probate -->

**58.** In relation to a Will “w”, s 13(1)(e) — the executors appointed by any will do not appear and extract probate means all with given x then not x's appeared and extracted probate and w's the executors appointed by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(1) — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted on failure of executors -->

**59.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Will “w” and a DATE “the date”, s 13(1) — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted on failure of executors if—

    (a) (a) no executor is appointed by a will;;

    (b) s 13(1)(a) — no executor is appointed by a will with w;

    (c) (b) the executor or all the executors appointed by will are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such;;

    (d) s 13(1)(b) — the executors are legally incapable of acting as such, or have renounced the right to act as such with w and the date;

    (e) (c) no executor survives the testator;;

    (f) s 13(1)(c) — no executor survives the testator with w;

    (g) (d) all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased; or;

    (h) s 13(1)(d) — all the executors die before obtaining probate or before having administered all the estate of the deceased with d and w;

    (i) (e) the executors appointed by any will do not appear and extract probate,; or

    (j) s 13(1)(e) — the executors appointed by any will do not appear and extract probate with w.

<!-- l4: declare:The rung of the class having a prior right to a grant under section 13(1) -->

**60.** In this Act, “The rung of the class having a prior right to a grant under section 13(1)” means one of the following—

    (a) “a universal or residuary legatee”;

    (b) “a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee”;

    (c) “such person or persons, being beneficiaries under the will, as would have been entitled to a grant of letters of administration if the deceased had died intestate”;

    (d) “a legatee having a beneficial interest”; or

    (e) “a creditor of the deceased”.

<!-- l4: decide:the dispositions to this person -->

**61.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a STRING “the reference”, the dispositions to this person means consider the case distinctions of d's the will :  when NOTHING has  then EMPTY. when JUST has w then filter with given dp then _ is the individual whose reference is _ with dp's the donee and the reference and w's the dispositions made by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(2)(a) — a universal or residuary legatee -->

**62.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a STRING “the reference”, s 13(2)(a) — a universal or residuary legatee means any with given dp then a universal or residuary gift with dp and the dispositions to this person with d and the reference.

<!-- l4: decide:a universal or residuary gift -->

**63.** In relation to a Disposition “dp”, a universal or residuary gift if—

    (a) dp's the kind of disposition is equal to a universal gift; or

    (b) dp's the kind of disposition is equal to a residuary gift.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(2)(d) — a legatee having a beneficial interest -->

**64.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a STRING “the reference”, s 13(2)(d) — a legatee having a beneficial interest means any with given dp then dp's beneficial and the dispositions to this person with d and the reference.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(2)(e) — a creditor of the deceased -->

**65.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a STRING “the reference”, s 13(2)(e) — a creditor of the deceased means any with given c then _ is the individual whose reference is _ with c's the creditor and the reference and d's the estate's the creditors of the deceased.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(2)(c) — a beneficiary under the will who would have been entitled to a grant on intestacy -->

**66.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a STRING “the reference”, s 13(2)(c) — a beneficiary under the will who would have been entitled to a grant on intestacy if—

    (a) being beneficiaries under the will,;

    (b) it is not the case that null with filter with given dp then dp's beneficial and the dispositions to this person with d and the reference;

    (c) as would have been entitled to a grant of letters of administration if the deceased had died intestate; and

    (d) s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin with d and the reference.

<!-- l4: decide:s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands -->

**67.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a STRING “the reference” and a BOOLEAN “the person is a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee”, s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands means if s 13(2)(a) — a universal or residuary legatee with d and the reference then JUST with a universal or residuary legatee if the person is a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee then JUST with a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee if s 13(2)(c) — a beneficiary under the will who would have been entitled to a grant on intestacy with d and the reference then JUST with such person or persons, being beneficiaries under the will, as would have been entitled to a grant of letters of administration if the deceased had died intestate if s 13(2)(d) — a legatee having a beneficial interest with d and the reference then JUST with a legatee having a beneficial interest if s 13(2)(e) — a creditor of the deceased with d and the reference then JUST with a creditor of the deceased otherwise NOTHING.

## Sections 14, 15, 17, 19 and 20 — grants to attorneys, and limited grants

<!-- l4: decide:another executor within Singapore willing to act -->

**68.** In relation to an Executor appointed by a will “x” and an Executor appointed by a will “y”, another executor within Singapore willing to act if—

    (a) y's the executor's the reference for this person is not equal to x's the executor's the reference for this person;

    (b) it is not the case that y's the executor's absent from Singapore; and

    (c) y's the executor's willing to act.

<!-- l4: decide:s 14 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to a duly authorised attorney of the absent executor -->

**69.** In relation to a Will “w” and an Executor appointed by a will “x”, s 14 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to a duly authorised attorney of the absent executor if—

    (a) Where an executor appointed by a will is absent from Singapore,;

    (b) x's the executor's absent from Singapore;

    (c) and there is no other executor within Singapore willing to act,; and

    (d) it is not the case that any with given y then another executor within Singapore willing to act with x and y and w's the executors appointed by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 14 — the limitation on a grant to the attorney of an absent executor -->

**70.** S 14 — the limitation on a grant to the attorney of an absent executor means limited in some other way with limited until he obtains probate for himself, and in the meantime to any purpose to which the attorney’s authority is limited.

<!-- l4: decide:s 15 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to the attorney of an absent person entitled -->

**71.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Will “w”, a Person “p”, a BOOLEAN “the person is a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee” and a DATE “the date”, s 15 — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted to the attorney of an absent person entitled if—

    (a) Where any person to whom letters of administration with the will annexed might be granted under section 13;

    (b) s 13(1) — letters of administration with the will annexed may be granted on failure of executors with d, w and the date;

    (c) isJust with s 13(2) — the rung of the prior-right class in which this person stands with d, p's the reference for this person and the person is a legal personal representative of a deceased universal or residuary legatee;

    (d) is absent from Singapore,; and

    (e) p's absent from Singapore.

<!-- l4: decide:s 17 — letters of administration may be granted, limited until the will is produced -->

**72.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “no will of the deceased is forthcoming” and a BOOLEAN “there is reason to believe that there is a will in existence”, s 17 — letters of administration may be granted, limited until the will is produced if—

    (a) no will of the deceased is forthcoming; and

    (b) there is reason to believe that there is a will in existence.

<!-- l4: decide:s 17 — the limitation on a grant until the will is produced -->

**73.** S 17 — the limitation on a grant until the will is produced means limited in some other way with limited until the will or an authenticated copy thereof is produced.

<!-- l4: decide:s 19 — letters of administration may be granted to an authorised attorney of the absent person -->

**74.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Person “p”, s 19 — letters of administration may be granted to an authorised attorney of the absent person if—

    (a) Where a person entitled to letters of administration in case of intestacy is absent from Singapore,;

    (b) s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin with d and p's the reference for this person;

    (c) p's absent from Singapore;

    (d) and no person equally entitled is willing to act,; and

    (e) any with given q then a person equally entitled who is not willing to act with p and q and the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a) with d.

<!-- l4: decide:a person equally entitled who is willing to act -->

**75.** In relation to a Person “p” and a Person “q”, a person equally entitled who is willing to act if—

    (a) q's the reference for this person is not equal to p's the reference for this person; and

    (b) q's willing to act.

<!-- l4: decide:s 19 — the limitation on a grant to the attorney of an absent person entitled -->

**76.** S 19 — the limitation on a grant to the attorney of an absent person entitled means limited in some other way with limited until he obtains a grant to himself.

<!-- l4: decide:s 20 — letters of administration may be granted pending a probate action -->

**77.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “a probate action is pending”, s 20 — letters of administration may be granted pending a probate action means a probate action is pending.

<!-- l4: decide:s 20 — the limitation on a grant pending a probate action -->

**78.** S 20 — the limitation on a grant pending a probate action means a grant that does not permit the distribution of the testator’s estate.

## Section 18 — Letters of administration on intestacy

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(1) — the person has died intestate -->

**79.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 18(1) — the person has died intestate means isNothing with d's the will.

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the trustees of the settlement -->

**80.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 18(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the trustees of the settlement if—

    (a) in regard to land settled previously to the death of the deceased,;

    (b) d's the estate's the value of land settled previously to the death of the deceased is greater than 0;

    (c) letters of administration may be granted to the trustees of the settlement.; and

    (d) it is not the case that null with d's the estate's the trustees of the settlement.

<!-- l4: decide:the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a) -->

**81.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a) means concat with list of the husband or widow of the deceased with d and the next of kin of the deceased with d.

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin -->

**82.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a STRING “the reference”, s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin means any with given p then p's the reference for this person is equal to the reference and the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a) with d.

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(4)(b) — such persons apply for letters of administration -->

**83.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 18(4)(b) — such persons apply for letters of administration means any with given a then an application by one of the section 18(4)(a) persons with d and a and d's the probate applications made in respect of the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:an application by one of the section 18(4)(a) persons -->

**84.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Probate application “a”, an application by one of the section 18(4)(a) persons means any with given p then _ is the individual whose reference is _ with a's the applicant and p's the reference for this person and the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a) with d.

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(4)(c) — no such person applies, and letters of administration may be granted to a creditor of the deceased -->

**85.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 18(4)(c) — no such person applies, and letters of administration may be granted to a creditor of the deceased if it is not the case that s 18(4)(b) — such persons apply for letters of administration with d.

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(4)(d)(i) — the next of kin, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire -->

**86.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 18(4)(d)(i) — the next of kin, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire if—

    (a) it is not the case that null with the next of kin of the deceased with d; and

    (b) the product of count with filter with given p then p's so desires that letters of administration be granted to such person as the court thinks fit and the next of kin of the deceased with d and 2 is greater than count with the next of kin of the deceased with d.

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(4)(d)(ii) — no next of kin or creditor or other person appears and makes out a claim to letters of administration -->

**87.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 18(4)(d)(ii) — no next of kin or creditor or other person appears and makes out a claim to letters of administration if d's a next of kin, creditor or other person does not have appeared and made out a claim to letters of administration.

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(4)(d) — letters of administration may be granted to such person as the court thinks fit -->

**88.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 18(4)(d) — letters of administration may be granted to such person as the court thinks fit if—

    (a) (i) the next of kin of any person dying intestate, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire; or;

    (b) s 18(4)(d)(i) — the next of kin, or the greater number of such next of kin, so desire with d;

    (c) (ii) no next of kin or creditor or other person appears and makes out a claim to letters of administration,; or

    (d) s 18(4)(d)(ii) — no next of kin or creditor or other person appears and makes out a claim to letters of administration with d.

<!-- l4: declare:A class to which letters of administration may be granted under section 18(4) -->

**89.** In this Act, “A class to which letters of administration may be granted under section 18(4)” means one of the following—

    (a) “the husband or widow or next of kin or any of them”;

    (b) “a creditor of the deceased, no such person having applied”; or

    (c) “such person as the court thinks fit”.

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(4) — the classes to which letters of administration may be granted -->

**90.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 18(4) — the classes to which letters of administration may be granted means concat with list of if not null with the persons entitled under section 18(4)(a) with d then list of the husband or widow or next of kin or any of them else EMPTY, if s 18(4)(c) — no such person applies, and letters of administration may be granted to a creditor of the deceased with d and not null with d's the estate's the creditors of the deceased then list of a creditor of the deceased, no such person having applied else EMPTY and if s 18(4)(d) — letters of administration may be granted to such person as the court thinks fit with d then list of such person as the court thinks fit else EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:s 18(5) — a law making special provision regarding the estates of persons of a particular religion or race is in evidence -->

**91.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 18(5) — a law making special provision regarding the estates of persons of a particular religion or race is in evidence if—

    (a) Nothing in this section shall affect any law by which special provision is made regarding the estates of persons of a particular religion or race.; and

    (b) d's a Muslim.

## Section 21 — Infants

<!-- l4: decide:s 21(1) — no probate or letters of administration shall be granted to a person while he is an infant -->

**92.** In relation to a Person “p” and a DATE “the date”, s 21(1) — no probate or letters of administration shall be granted to a person while he is an infant means _ is an infant on _ with p and the date.

<!-- l4: decide:s 21(2) — this infant would, but for his infancy, be entitled to probate or letters of administration -->

**93.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, an Infant “i” and a DATE “the date”, s 21(2) — this infant would, but for his infancy, be entitled to probate or letters of administration if—

    (a) _ is an infant on _ with i's the infant and the date; and

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) s 8(1) — probate may be granted to this person as an executor appointed by a will with d and i's the infant's the reference for this person; or

        (ii) s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin with d and i's the infant's the reference for this person.

<!-- l4: decide:the infant executors or persons so entitled -->

**94.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, the infant executors or persons so entitled means filter with given i then s 21(2) — this infant would, but for his infancy, be entitled to probate or letters of administration with d, i and the date and d's the infants concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:is this guardian of the person and property of the infant -->

**95.** In relation to a Grantee “gr” and a Guardian “gu”, is this guardian of the person and property of the infant if—

    (a) gu's of the person or of the property is equal to guardian of the person and property of the infant;

    (b) it is not the case that gu's removed from his guardianship by the court; and

    (c) _ is the individual whose reference is _ with gr's the grantee and gu's the guardian's the reference for this person.

<!-- l4: decide:s 21(2) — this grant is made to the guardian of the person and property of an infant so entitled -->

**96.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grantee “gr” and a DATE “the date”, s 21(2) — this grant is made to the guardian of the person and property of an infant so entitled if—

    (a) gr's the capacity in which the grant is made is equal to as the guardian of the person and property of the infant; and

    (b) consider the case distinctions of gr's the reference for the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has r then any with given i then i's the infant's the reference for this person is equal to r and s 21(2) — this infant would, but for his infancy, be entitled to probate or letters of administration with d, i and the date and any with given gu then _ is this guardian of the person and property of the infant _ with gr and gu and i's the guardians of the infant and d's the infants concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant -->

**97.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grant “g” and a DATE “the date”, s 21(2) — letters of administration may be granted to the guardian of the person and property of the infant if—

    (a) Where an infant would, but for his infancy, be entitled to probate or letters of administration,;

    (b) it is not the case that null with the infant executors or persons so entitled with d and the date;

    (c) letters of administration with or without the will annexed may, subject to section 6(1), be granted;

    (d) any of the following applies—

        (i) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration; or

        (ii) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration with the will annexed;

    (e) it is not the case that s 6(1) — granted to more than 4 persons in respect of the same property with g;

    (f) to the guardian of the person and property of the infant,;

    (g) any with given gr then s 21(2) — this grant is made to the guardian of the person and property of an infant so entitled with d, gr and the date and g's the grantees;

    (h) limited until the infant obtains a grant to himself.; and

    (i) g's the limitation is equal to s 21 — the limitation on a grant made under subsection (2) with d and the date.

<!-- l4: decide:s 21(3) — there are 2 or more infant executors or persons so entitled -->

**98.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 21(3) — there are 2 or more infant executors or persons so entitled means count with the infant executors or persons so entitled with d and the date is at least 2.

<!-- l4: decide:s 21 — the limitation on a grant made under subsection (2) -->

**99.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 21 — the limitation on a grant made under subsection (2) means if s 21(3) — there are 2 or more infant executors or persons so entitled with d and the date, then limited in some other way with limited until any of them obtains a grant; otherwise, limited in some other way with limited until the infant obtains a grant to himself.

## Section 22 — Persons who lack mental capacity

<!-- l4: decide:s 22(1) — no probate or letters of administration are to be granted to a person who lacks mental capacity -->

**100.** In relation to a Person “p”, s 22(1) — no probate or letters of administration are to be granted to a person who lacks mental capacity means p's lacks mental capacity (within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act 2008) to make decisions with respect to the management and administration of the person's property and affairs.

<!-- l4: decide:s 22(2) — this person would, if he or she did not lack mental capacity, be entitled to probate or letters of administration -->

**101.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Person “p”, s 22(2) — this person would, if he or she did not lack mental capacity, be entitled to probate or letters of administration if—

    (a) s 22(1) — no probate or letters of administration are to be granted to a person who lacks mental capacity with p; and

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) s 8(1) — probate may be granted to this person as an executor appointed by a will with d and p's the reference for this person; or

        (ii) s 18(4)(a) — one of the husband or widow or next of kin with d and p's the reference for this person.

<!-- l4: decide:s 22(2) — the limitation on a grant made for the use and benefit of a person who lacks mental capacity -->

**102.** S 22(2) — the limitation on a grant made for the use and benefit of a person who lacks mental capacity means limited in some other way with until that person ceases to lack mental capacity and obtains a grant to himself or herself.

## Sections 23 to 27 — limited grants, accrual, exception and expiry

<!-- l4: decide:s 23 — letters of administration limited to trust property may be granted -->

**103.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 23 — letters of administration limited to trust property may be granted if—

    (a) Where a person dies, leaving property in which he had no beneficial interest on his own account,;

    (b) the sum of d's the estate's the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore and d's the estate's the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated outside Singapore is greater than 0;

    (c) and does not leave a representative who is able and willing to act,; and

    (d) s 23 — the deceased leaves a representative who is not able and willing to act with d and the date.

<!-- l4: decide:s 23 — the deceased leaves a representative who is able and willing to act -->

**104.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 23 — the deceased leaves a representative who is able and willing to act if—

    (a) any with given gr then a representative willing to act with gr and the personal representatives of the estate with d; or

    (b) any with given x then an executor whose appointment stands and who is willing to act with x and the date and the executors appointed by the will of the deceased with d.

<!-- l4: decide:an executor whose appointment stands and who is willing to act -->

**105.** In relation to an Executor appointed by a will “x” and a DATE “the date”, an executor whose appointment stands and who is willing to act if—

    (a) it is not the case that has died with x's the executor;

    (b) s 13(1)(b) — this executor is not disqualified with x and the date; and

    (c) x's the executor's willing to act.

<!-- l4: decide:the executors appointed by the will of the deceased -->

**106.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, the executors appointed by the will of the deceased means consider the case distinctions of d's the will :  when NOTHING has  then EMPTY. when JUST has w then w's the executors appointed by the will.

<!-- l4: decide:a representative willing to act -->

**107.** In relation to a Grantee “gr”, a representative willing to act means consider the case distinctions of the individual in with gr's the grantee :  when JUST has p then not has died with p and p's willing to act. when NOTHING has  then TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:s 23 — the limitation on a grant of trust property -->

**108.** S 23 — the limitation on a grant of trust property means limited to settled land or to trust property.

<!-- l4: decide:s 24 — the limitation on a grant to collect and preserve property -->

**109.** S 24 — the limitation on a grant to collect and preserve property means a grant that does not permit the distribution of the testator’s estate.

<!-- l4: declare:To whom the representation of the estate accrues on the death of one of several personal representatives -->

**110.** In this Act, “To whom the representation of the estate accrues on the death of one of several personal representatives” means one of the following—

    (a) “section 25(1) does not apply”;

    (b) “the representation of the estate accrues to the surviving executor or executors”;

    (c) “the representation of the estate accrues to the surviving administrator or administrators”; or

    (d) “the representation does not accrue, this being a case to which section 6 applies”.

<!-- l4: decide:s 25(1) — death of one of several executors or administrators -->

**111.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grant “g” and a DATE “the date”, s 25(1) — death of one of several executors or administrators means if not count with g's the grantees is greater than 1 and any with given gr then this grantee has died with gr and g's the grantees then section 25(1) does not apply if g's the kind of grant is equal to probate then the representation of the estate accrues to the surviving executor or executors if s 6(2) — the requirement as to the grantees is engaged with d and the date then the representation does not accrue, this being a case to which section 6 applies otherwise the representation of the estate accrues to the surviving administrator or administrators.

<!-- l4: decide:this grantee has died -->

**112.** In relation to a Grantee “gr”, this grantee has died means consider the case distinctions of the individual in with gr's the grantee :  when JUST has p then has died with p. when NOTHING has  then FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:s 25(2) — letters of administration may be granted in respect of any estate not fully administered -->

**113.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Grant “g”, s 25(2) — letters of administration may be granted in respect of any estate not fully administered if—

    (a) On the death of an administrator,;

    (b) any with given gr then gr's the capacity in which the grant is made is equal to as administrator and this grantee has died with gr and g's the grantees;

    (c) letters of administration may be granted in respect of any estate not fully administered; and

    (d) it is not the case that d's the estate's fully administered.

<!-- l4: decide:s 26(2) — a further grant may be made of the part of the estate excepted -->

**114.** In relation to a Grant “g”, s 26(2) — a further grant may be made of the part of the estate excepted means isJust with g's the exception subject to which the grant is made.

<!-- l4: decide:s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted to those persons to whom original grants might have been made -->

**115.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Grant “g”, s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted to those persons to whom original grants might have been made if—

    (a) When a limited grant;

    (b) g's the limitation is not equal to not limited;

    (c) has expired by effluxion of time or the happening of the event or contingency on which it was limited,;

    (d) g's expired by effluxion of time or by the happening of the event or contingency on which it was limited;

    (e) and there is still some part of the deceased’s estate unadministered,; and

    (f) it is not the case that d's the estate's fully administered.

# Part 5 — Security

<!-- l4: declare:The security required on a grant -->

**116.** In this Act, “The security required on a grant” means one of the following—

    (a) “no security is required”;

    (b) “security by bond in the prescribed form by the grantee and 2 sureties”, having a “the amount of the bond” (a Money); or

    (c) “security by bond in the prescribed form by the grantee, sureties being dispensed with”, having a “the amount of the bond” (a Money).

<!-- l4: decide:s 29(2) — the amount at which the estate within the jurisdiction is sworn -->

**117.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 29(2) — the amount at which the estate within the jurisdiction is sworn means the difference between sum with map with given c then c's the debt and filter with given c then c's secured and d's the estate's the creditors of the deceased and the value of the property in Singapore with d's the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:s 29(4) — this grantee is the Public Trustee -->

**118.** In relation to a Grantee “gr”, s 29(4) — this grantee is the Public Trustee means gr's the grantee is equal to the Public Trustee.

<!-- l4: decide:s 29(8)(a) — the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made is an infant -->

**119.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grantee “gr” and a DATE “the date”, s 29(8)(a) — the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made is an infant means consider the case distinctions of gr's the reference for the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has r then any with given i then i's the infant's the reference for this person is equal to r and _ is an infant on _ with i's the infant and the date and d's the infants concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security -->

**120.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grant “g”, a Grantee “gr”, a The further facts on which the grant machinery turns “f” and a DATE “the date”, s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security if—

    (a) A grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court;

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration; or

        (ii) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration with the will annexed;

    (c) the grant was made by a Family Court with g;

    (d) shall not be required to give security for the due administration of the estate unless —; and

    (e) none of the following applies—

        (i) (a) the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made is an infant; or;

        (ii) s 29(8)(a) — the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made is an infant with d, gr and the date;

        (iii) (b) the Family Court thinks fit to require such security.; or

        (iv) f's the Family Court thinks fit to require such security.

<!-- l4: decide:the grant was made by a Family Court -->

**121.** In relation to a Grant “g”, the grant was made by a Family Court means consider the case distinctions of g's the court that made the grant :  when a court within the meaning of these Acts has c then c is equal to a Family Court. in any other case FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee -->

**122.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grant “g”, a Grantee “gr”, a The further facts on which the grant machinery turns “f” and a DATE “the date”, s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee means if not g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration or g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration with the will annexed then no security is required if s 29(4) — this grantee is the Public Trustee with gr then no security is required if s 29(8) — this grantee of letters of administration from a Family Court shall not be required to give security with d, g, gr, f and the date then no security is required if f's the administrator is entitled to the whole of the estate after payment of the debts then security by bond in the prescribed form by the grantee, sureties being dispensed with with s 29(2) — the amount at which the estate within the jurisdiction is sworn with d otherwise security by bond in the prescribed form by the grantee and 2 sureties with s 29(2) — the amount at which the estate within the jurisdiction is sworn with d.

<!-- l4: decide:security is lawfully required of some grantee -->

**123.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grant “g”, a The further facts on which the grant machinery turns “f” and a DATE “the date”, security is lawfully required of some grantee means any with given gr then security is lawfully required of this grantee with d, g, gr, f and the date and g's the grantees.

<!-- l4: decide:security is lawfully required of this grantee -->

**124.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grant “g”, a Grantee “gr”, a The further facts on which the grant machinery turns “f” and a DATE “the date”, security is lawfully required of this grantee means consider the case distinctions of s 29 — the security ordinarily required of this grantee with d, g, gr, f and the date :  when no security is required has  then FALSE. in any other case TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:s 30 — letters of administration are granted to a creditor -->

**125.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Grant “g”, s 30 — letters of administration are granted to a creditor if—

    (a) any of the following applies—

        (i) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration; or

        (ii) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration with the will annexed; and

    (b) any with given gr then s 13(2)(e) — a creditor of the deceased with d and the reference of the grantee with gr and g's the grantees.

# Part 8 — District Courts

<!-- l4: decide:ss 34 and 36 — repealed, and therefore not encoded -->

**126.** Ss 34 and 36 — repealed, and therefore not encoded if—

    (a) 34. [Repealed by Act 27 of 2014]; and

    (b) 36. [Repealed by Act 27 of 2014].

<!-- l4: decide:s 35(1) — the saving in section 35(1) applies to this grant -->

**127.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Grant “g”, s 35(1) — the saving in section 35(1) applies to this grant if—

    (a) No probate or letters of administration granted by a District Court before 1 January 2015;

    (b) g's the court that made the grant is equal to a District Court, the grant having been made before 1 January 2015;

    (c) shall be invalid by reason of the assets and effects of the deceased being subsequently found to be of a value which exceeds $3 million.; and

    (d) the value of the whole estate with d's the estate is greater than 3000000.

<!-- l4: decide:the value of the whole estate -->

**128.** In relation to an Estate “e”, the value of the whole estate means the sum of the sum of the sum of e's the value of the movable property situated in Singapore and e's the value of the immovable property situated in Singapore and e's the value of the movable property situated outside Singapore and e's the value of the immovable property situated outside Singapore.

# Part 11 — General

## Section 55 — Grant to the Public Trustee in cases of delay

<!-- l4: decide:s 55(1)(a) — six months have expired from the death and no application has been made -->

**129.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 55(1)(a) — six months have expired from the death and no application has been made if—

    (a) six months have expired from the death with d and the date; and

    (b) null with d's the probate applications made in respect of the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:six months have expired from the death -->

**130.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, six months have expired from the death means consider the case distinctions of the date of death of with d's the deceased :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has dd then _ is before _ with add months with dd and 6 and the date.

<!-- l4: decide:s 55(1)(b) — an application made within the 6 months has not been proceeded with, or has been withdrawn or refused -->

**131.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 55(1)(b) — an application made within the 6 months has not been proceeded with, or has been withdrawn or refused means any with given a then an application within the six months that came to nothing with d and a and d's the probate applications made in respect of the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:an application within the six months that came to nothing -->

**132.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Probate application “a”, an application within the six months that came to nothing if—

    (a) the application was made within 6 months of the death with d and a; and

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) has not within that period been proceeded with,;

        (ii) a's what became of the application is equal to not proceeded with;

        (iii) or has been withdrawn;

        (iv) a's what became of the application is equal to withdrawn;

        (v) or refused; or

        (vi) a's what became of the application is equal to refused.

<!-- l4: decide:the application was made within 6 months of the death -->

**133.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Probate application “a”, the application was made within 6 months of the death means consider the case distinctions of a's the date of the application :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has da then consider the case distinctions of the date of death of with d's the deceased :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has dd then not _ is after _ with da and add months with dd and 6.

<!-- l4: decide:s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish -->

**134.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grant “g”, a The further facts on which the grant machinery turns “f” and a DATE “the date”, s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish if—

    (a) where any person, who has received a grant of letters of administration with or without the will annexed,;

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration; or

        (ii) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration with the will annexed;

    (c) to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish;

    (d) security is lawfully required of some grantee with d, g, f and the date;

    (e) g's has given such security as is not lawfully required to be furnished;

    (f) neglects within one month of the date of the grant; and

    (g) one month has expired from the date of the grant with g and the date.

<!-- l4: decide:one month has expired from the date of the grant -->

**135.** In relation to a Grant “g” and a DATE “the date”, one month has expired from the date of the grant means consider the case distinctions of g's the date of the grant :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has dg then _ is before _ with add months with dg and 1 and the date.

<!-- l4: decide:s 55(1)(d) — a receiver may be appointed under section 39, but the appointment would not be a sufficient protection -->

**136.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a The further facts on which the grant machinery turns “f”, s 55(1)(d) — a receiver may be appointed under section 39, but the appointment would not be a sufficient protection if—

    (a) Where any person dies leaving property within Singapore;

    (b) the value of the property in Singapore with d's the estate is greater than 0;

    (c) that there is danger that the property may be wasted,;

    (d) f's there is danger that the property may be wasted;

    (e) but it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate;; and

    (f) f's it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:s 55(1)(e) — an administrator has failed to extract the grant of letters of administration -->

**137.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 55(1)(e) — an administrator has failed to extract the grant of letters of administration means any with given g then a grant of letters of administration that has not been extracted with g and d's the grants made in respect of the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:a grant of letters of administration that has not been extracted -->

**138.** In relation to a Grant “g”, a grant of letters of administration that has not been extracted if—

    (a) any of the following applies—

        (i) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration; or

        (ii) g's the kind of grant is equal to letters of administration with the will annexed; and

    (b) g's does not have been extracted.

<!-- l4: decide:s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made -->

**139.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made if—

    (a) it is not the case that null with the personal representatives of the estate with d;

    (b) all with given gr then this grantee has died with gr and the personal representatives of the estate with d;

    (c) six months have elapsed since the last of the representatives died with d and the date; and

    (d) null with d's the probate applications made in respect of the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:six months have elapsed since the last of the representatives died -->

**140.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, six months have elapsed since the last of the representatives died means all with given gr then six months have elapsed since this grantee died with gr and the date and the personal representatives of the estate with d.

<!-- l4: decide:six months have elapsed since this grantee died -->

**141.** In relation to a Grantee “gr” and a DATE “the date”, six months have elapsed since this grantee died means consider the case distinctions of the individual in with gr's the grantee :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has p then consider the case distinctions of the date of death of with p :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has dp then _ is before _ with add months with dp and 6 and the date.

<!-- l4: decide:s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay -->

**142.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, a Grant “g”, a The further facts on which the grant machinery turns “f” and a DATE “the date”, s 55(1) — letters of administration may be granted to the Public Trustee in a case of delay if—

    (a) (a) where, after the expiration of 6 months from the death of a deceased person, no application has been made for probate or letters of administration to his estate;;

    (b) s 55(1)(a) — six months have expired from the death and no application has been made with d and the date;

    (c) (b) where any such application, though made within the said 6 months, has not within that period been proceeded with, or has been withdrawn or refused;;

    (d) s 55(1)(b) — an application made within the 6 months has not been proceeded with, or has been withdrawn or refused with d;

    (e) (c) where any person, who has received a grant of letters of administration with or without the will annexed, neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish;;

    (f) s 55(1)(c) — the grantee neglects within one month of the date of the grant to give such security as he is lawfully required to furnish with d, g, f and the date;

    (g) (d) where a receiver may be appointed under section 39, but it appears that such appointment would not be a sufficient protection for the estate;;

    (h) s 55(1)(d) — a receiver may be appointed under section 39, but the appointment would not be a sufficient protection with d and f;

    (i) (e) where an administrator has failed to extract the grant of letters of administration; or;

    (j) s 55(1)(e) — an administrator has failed to extract the grant of letters of administration with d;

    (k) (f) where after the death of a last surviving executor or administrator of a deceased person’s estate 6 months have elapsed and no application for the representation of the estate has been made,; or

    (l) s 55(1)(f) — six months have elapsed since the death of a last surviving executor or administrator, and no application has been made with d and the date.

<!-- l4: decide:s 55(2) — the six-month periods do not prevent the Public Trustee from applying sooner -->

**143.** S 55(2) — the six-month periods do not prevent the Public Trustee from applying sooner means Nothing in this section shall be construed so as to prevent the Public Trustee from applying for or being granted letters of administration of the estate of a deceased person with or without the will annexed before the expiration of a period of 6 months of the death of the deceased..

## Section 56(2) — the $500 route where no administration has been taken out

<!-- l4: decide:s 56(2) — the assets of the deceased, including the funds directed to be paid -->

**144.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 56(2) — the assets of the deceased, including the funds directed to be paid means the sum of the value of the whole estate with d's the estate and d's the estate's the amount of the funds in court directed to be paid, transferred or delivered to him.

<!-- l4: decide:the persons named in section 56(2) -->

**145.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, the persons named in section 56(2) means concat with list of the husband or widow of the deceased with d and filter with given p then _ survives _ with p and d's the deceased and concat with list of map with given c then c's the child and d's the deceased's children, maybeToList with d's the family's the father of the deceased, maybeToList with d's the family's the mother of the deceased and map with given r then r's the relative and d's the family's the brothers and sisters of the deceased.

<!-- l4: decide:s 56(2) — the funds may be paid to this person on a declaration in the prescribed form -->

**146.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a STRING “the reference”, s 56(2) — the funds may be paid to this person on a declaration in the prescribed form if—

    (a) If no administration has been taken out to the estate of such deceased person;

    (b) null with d's the grants made in respect of the estate;

    (c) who has died intestate,;

    (d) s 18(1) — the person has died intestate with d;

    (e) and whose assets do not exceed $500, including the amount of the funds directed to be so paid, transferred or delivered to him,;

    (f) s 56(2) — the assets of the deceased, including the funds directed to be paid with d is at most 500;

    (g) the funds may be paid, transferred or delivered to the person who, being a widower, widow, child, father, mother, brother or sister of the deceased,; and

    (h) any with given p then p's the reference for this person is equal to the reference and the persons named in section 56(2) with d.

## Section 62 — Administration by the Public Trustee

<!-- l4: decide:s 62(2)(b) — the deceased died on or after 17 September 2005 -->

**147.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 62(2)(b) — the deceased died on or after 17 September 2005 means consider the case distinctions of the date of death of with d's the deceased :  when NOTHING has  then FALSE. when JUST has dd then not _ is before _ with dd and YMD with 2005, 9 and 17.

<!-- l4: decide:s 62 — the value of the property in Singapore for the purposes of section 62 -->

**148.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 62 — the value of the property in Singapore for the purposes of section 62 means the difference between if s 62(2)(b) — the deceased died on or after 17 September 2005 with d then d's the estate's the value of any moneys payable by an appointed insurer pursuant to the Dependants’ Protection Insurance Scheme or any other equivalent scheme maintained by the Central Provident Fund Board else 0 and the difference between d's the estate's the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore and the value of the property in Singapore with d's the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property -->

**149.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 62(1) — the Public Trustee may declare that he undertakes to administer the property if—

    (a) Where any person dies leaving property in Singapore not exceeding $50,000 in value (without deduction for debts),;

    (b) s 62 — the value of the property in Singapore for the purposes of section 62 with d is at most 50000;

    (c) after satisfying himself that no application for letters of administration is pending,; and

    (d) it is not the case that any with given a then a pending application for letters of administration with a and d's the probate applications made in respect of the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:a pending application for letters of administration -->

**150.** In relation to a Probate application “a”, a pending application for letters of administration if—

    (a) any of the following applies—

        (i) a's the grant applied for is equal to letters of administration; or

        (ii) a's the grant applied for is equal to letters of administration with the will annexed; and

    (b) a's what became of the application is equal to still pending.

<!-- l4: decide:s 62(3) — the Public Trustee is empowered to administer the property as though letters of administration had been granted to him -->

**151.** In relation to a The further facts on which the grant machinery turns “f”, s 62(3) — the Public Trustee is empowered to administer the property as though letters of administration had been granted to him means f's the Public Trustee has by writing signed by him declared that he undertakes to administer such property.

## Section 63 — Payment for a minor’s maintenance out of property held by the Public Trustee

<!-- l4: declare:The payments the Public Trustee may make for a minor’s maintenance under section 63 -->

**152.** In this Act, “The payments the Public Trustee may make for a minor’s maintenance under section 63” means one of the following—

    (a) “no payment may be made under section 63”;

    (b) “payments of the whole or such part of the income and capital money of such property as may in all the circumstances be reasonable”; or

    (c) “payments of capital money to the extent of $25,000”.

<!-- l4: decide:s 63(1) — the property is held upon trust for a person during whose minority payments may be made -->

**153.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 63(1) — the property is held upon trust for a person during whose minority payments may be made means any with given i then _ is an infant on _ with i's the infant and the date and d's the infants concerned in the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:s 63 — the payments the Public Trustee may make -->

**154.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a DATE “the date”, s 63 — the payments the Public Trustee may make means if not s 63(1) — the property is held upon trust for a person during whose minority payments may be made with d and the date then no payment may be made under section 63 if d's the estate's the value of the property administered by the Public Trustee is at most 25000 then payments of the whole or such part of the income and capital money of such property as may in all the circumstances be reasonable if d's the estate's the value of the property administered by the Public Trustee is at most 50000 then payments of capital money to the extent of $25,000 otherwise no payment may be made under section 63.

## Section 64(1) — the $10,000 exemption from notice of distribution

<!-- l4: decide:s 64(1) — the total value of the property administered by the Public Trustee -->

**155.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 64(1) — the total value of the property administered by the Public Trustee means the difference between d's the estate's the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated outside Singapore and the difference between d's the estate's the value of any property which the deceased possessed or was entitled to as trustee and not beneficially, situated in Singapore and d's the estate's the value of the property administered by the Public Trustee.

<!-- l4: decide:s 64(1) — it shall not be necessary for the Public Trustee to give notice of his intention to distribute the estate -->

**156.** In relation to a Deceased person “d”, s 64(1) — it shall not be necessary for the Public Trustee to give notice of his intention to distribute the estate means s 64(1) — the total value of the property administered by the Public Trustee with d is at most 10000.

# The Act’s own “shall” and “may” — the deontic outcomes

<!-- l4: declare:A party under the Probate and Administration Act -->

**157.** In this Act, “A party under the Probate and Administration Act” means one of the following—

    (a) “the court”;

    (b) “the registrar”; or

    (c) “the grantee”.

<!-- l4: declare:An act under the Probate and Administration Act -->

**158.** In this Act, “An act under the Probate and Administration Act” means one of the following—

    (a) “take an oath in the prescribed form, faithfully to administer the estate and to account for the same”;

    (b) “give security for the due administration of the estate”;

    (c) “revoke the probate and grant a new probate of the will and codicil together”;

    (d) “grant letters of administration to those persons to whom original grants might have been made”; or

    (e) “grant letters of administration with or without the will annexed to the Public Trustee”.

<!-- l4: decide:s 28(2) — the grantee is the Public Trustee or a trust company -->

**159.** In relation to a Person or corporation “pc”, s 28(2) — the grantee is the Public Trustee or a trust company means consider the case distinctions of pc :  when the Public Trustee has  then TRUE. when a corporation licensed as a trust company under the Trust Companies Act 2005 has n then TRUE. in any other case FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:s 28 — the grantee shall take an oath -->

**160.** In relation to a Grantee “gr”, s 28 — the grantee shall take an oath means if s 28(2) — the grantee is the Public Trustee or a trust company with gr's the grantee, then FULFILLED; otherwise, the grantee must take an oath in the prescribed form, faithfully to administer the estate and to account for the same..

<!-- l4: decide:s 29(7) — the grantee shall give security for the due administration of the estate -->

**161.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “security is required”, s 29(7) — the grantee shall give security for the due administration of the estate means if security is required, then the grantee must give security for the due administration of the estate, within 30. Failing which, the court may grant letters of administration with or without the will annexed to the Public Trustee, within 30..; otherwise, FULFILLED.

<!-- l4: decide:s 12(2) — the probate shall be revoked and a new probate granted -->

**162.** In relation to a The consequence of a codicil propounded after a grant “the consequence”, s 12(2) — the probate shall be revoked and a new probate granted means if the consequence is equal to the probate shall be revoked, and a new probate shall be granted of the will and codicil together, then the court must revoke the probate and grant a new probate of the will and codicil together.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

<!-- l4: decide:s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted -->

**163.** In relation to a Deceased person “d” and a Grant “g”, s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted means if s 27 — letters of administration shall be granted to those persons to whom original grants might have been made with d and g, then the court must grant letters of administration to those persons to whom original grants might have been made.; otherwise, FULFILLED.

