## Constructors

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA person in full -->

**165.** In relation to a STRING “the name”, a STRING “the reference”, a Vital status “the vital status”, an optional DATE “the date of majority”, a list of Child “the children of the person”, a BOOLEAN “does lack mental capacity”, a BOOLEAN “is absent from Singapore”, a BOOLEAN “is willing to act” and a BOOLEAN “does so desire”, a PAA person in full means Person where name is the name, the reference for this person is the reference, date of birth is NOTHING, vital status is the vital status, children is the children of the person, at the date of the death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive is FALSE, money or other property given, paid or settled by the intestate during his life to or for the advancement of the person is 0, the date on which the person attains the age of majority is the date of majority, a soldier being in actual military service is FALSE, a mariner or seaman being at sea is FALSE, a member of any naval or marine forces so circumstanced that if he were a soldier he would be in actual military service is FALSE, so desires that letters of administration be granted to such person as the court thinks fit is does so desire, lacks mental capacity (within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act 2008) to make decisions with respect to the management and administration of the person's property and affairs is does lack mental capacity, absent from Singapore is is absent from Singapore and willing to act is is willing to act.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA adult -->

**166.** In relation to a STRING “the name” and a STRING “the reference”, a PAA adult means a PAA person in full with the name, the reference, living, JUST with YMD with 2005, 1 and 1, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA minor -->

**167.** In relation to a STRING “the name” and a STRING “the reference”, a PAA minor means a PAA person in full with the name, the reference, living, JUST with YMD with 2032, 6 and 1, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA person of unknown age -->

**168.** In relation to a STRING “the name” and a STRING “the reference”, a PAA person of unknown age means a PAA person in full with the name, the reference, living, NOTHING, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA legitimate child -->

**169.** In relation to a Person “p”, a PAA legitimate child means Child where the child is p, a legitimate child of the person whose child he is is TRUE and adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA adopted child -->

**170.** In relation to a Person “p”, a PAA adopted child means Child where the child is p, a legitimate child of the person whose child he is is FALSE and adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam is TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA child neither legitimate nor adopted -->

**171.** In relation to a Person “p”, a PAA child neither legitimate nor adopted means Child where the child is p, a legitimate child of the person whose child he is is FALSE and adopted by that person by virtue of an order of court under any written law for the time being in force in Singapore, Malaysia or Brunei Darussalam is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA marriage to -->

**172.** In relation to a Person “p” and a BOOLEAN “subsisting”, a PAA marriage to means Marriage where the spouse is p, the date of the solemnisation of the marriage is JUST with YMD with 1990, 5 and 1 and subsisting at the death of the deceased, in the sense of not dissolved or annulled before the death is subsisting.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA family -->

**173.** In relation to a list of Marriage “the marriages” and a list of Collateral relative “the siblings”, a PAA family means Family where the marriages of the deceased is the marriages, the father of the deceased is NOTHING, the mother of the deceased is NOTHING, the brothers and sisters of the deceased is the siblings, the grandparents of the deceased is EMPTY and the uncles and aunts of the deceased is EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA sibling of the whole blood -->

**174.** In relation to a Person “p”, a PAA sibling of the whole blood means Collateral relative where the relative is p and of the whole blood or of the half blood is of the whole blood.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA executor -->

**175.** In relation to a Person “p”, a BOOLEAN “is incapable otherwise”, a BOOLEAN “has renounced”, a BOOLEAN “has extracted probate” and a BOOLEAN “has administered the estate”, a PAA executor means Executor appointed by a will where the executor is p, the appointment, express or implied is express, legally incapable of acting as such, otherwise than under section 21(1) or section 22(1) is is incapable otherwise, has renounced the right to act as such is has renounced, appeared and extracted probate is has extracted probate and has administered all the estate of the deceased is has administered the estate.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA gift to -->

**176.** In relation to a Person “p”, a Kind of disposition “the kind”, a Money “the value” and a BOOLEAN “is beneficial”, a PAA gift to means Disposition where the donee is an individual with p, the kind of disposition is the kind, the value of the disposition is the value, beneficial is is beneficial and not determinable at or before the death of the donee is TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA life interest to -->

**177.** In relation to a Person “p”, a PAA life interest to means Life interest where the life tenant is p and the value of the property in which the life interest subsists is 10000.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA will of -->

**178.** In relation to a Person “t”, a list of Executor appointed by a will “the executors”, a list of Disposition “the dispositions” and a list of Life interest “the life interests”, a PAA will of means Will where the testator is t, the date of execution is JUST with YMD with 2020, 3 and 1, in writing is TRUE, signed at the foot or end thereof by the testator is TRUE, signed at the foot or end thereof by some other person in his presence and by his direction is FALSE, the signature made or acknowledged by the testator as the signature to his will or codicil in the presence of 2 or more witnesses present at the same time is TRUE, apparent on the face of the will that the testator intended to give effect by such his signature to the writing signed as his will is TRUE, the attesting witnesses is EMPTY, the executors appointed by the will is the executors, the guardians of infant children appointed by the will is EMPTY, the dispositions made by the will is the dispositions, expressed to be made in contemplation of a marriage is FALSE, the reference for the person with whom the marriage contemplated was to be solemnised is NOTHING, made in exercise of a power of appointment is FALSE, the estate thereby appointed would not in default of such appointment pass to his or her heir, executor or administrator or the person entitled under the Intestate Succession Act 1967 is FALSE, the life interests arising under the will is the life interests, it appears by the will that the personal representative is entitled to take that part beneficially is FALSE and the codicils is EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA grantee -->

**179.** In relation to a Person or corporation “pc”, a Capacity in which the grant is made “the capacity” and an optional STRING “for whose benefit”, a PAA grantee means Grantee where the grantee is pc, the capacity in which the grant is made is the capacity and the reference for the person for whose use and benefit the grant is made is for whose benefit.

<!-- l4: decide:a PAA grant -->

